# Roles most associated with requirements work in ML-enabled systems

Data: `data/requirements_engineering_for_ML-enabled_systems.csv` (276 respondents x 202 columns).
Code: `analysis/01_inspect.py`, `analysis/02_main_analysis.py` (seed=20261025, B=10,000).
Outputs: `analysis/02_results_table.csv`, `analysis/02_results.json`, `analysis/02_main_analysis_output.txt`.

## Answer (hypothesis)
**Project Lead / Project Manager** and **Data Scientist** are the two roles most associated with
requirements work in ML-enabled systems: 51.031% (95% bootstrap CI 43.81-58.25; BCa 43.30-57.22)
and 48.969% (95% CI 42.27-56.19; BCa 41.75-55.67) of the 194 respondents who completed the
role-question block said that ML aspects of their projects are addressed by these roles
(Q8_ML_Addressing_* == "quoted"), versus <=25.8% for every other role. The pair is the top-2 in
9/9 pre-registered specifications and in 100% of 10,000 bootstrap replicates.

## Primary (pre-registered) specification
* unit = respondent (one row each, IDs unique); Q8 refers to the respondent's organisation, so no
  per-project expansion;
* outcome = share with `Q8_ML_Addressing_<role> == "quoted"` (the block is a multiple-choice
  question in the raw file: only {quoted, not quoted, -77}; there is no "high/extreme degree"
  threshold available for Q8);
* denominator = complete case within the block, n = 194 (82 non-responders, all Status=Suspended);
* cleaning = -99/-77/-66/-1 -> missing (matches the researcher's confirmed context), "0" in
  categorical columns -> missing, "I don't know" -> missing;
* bootstrap = 10,000 respondent resamples, one shared index vector for all 8 columns, seed 20261025,
  percentile CI primary, BCa reported.

